  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian government is actively coordinating efforts across various sectors to ensure national food security. Perum Bulog is currently working to stabilize rice supplies by optimizing the absorption of domestic harvests from farmers. This initiative aligns with broader inter-ministerial strategies, including the collaboration between the Ministry of Public Works and the Ministry of Agriculture to enhance irrigation infrastructure and distribute water pumps to improve farming productivity. Furthermore, officials are exploring diverse avenues to support self-sufficiency, such as the strategic use of coastal spatial planning and regional agricultural development. These efforts occur against a backdrop of global challenges, where international conflicts in the Middle East and Ukraine have impacted food distribution channels and escalated operational costs for humanitarian organizations like the World Food Programme, leading to concerns over potential reductions in global food assistance.",
